WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:07.310
The first thing you need to analyze is,
is your company ready for change?

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.760
Is your company willing to look
at new ways of doing things?

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:16.824
&gt;&gt; This program, transformational
leadership, was designed specifically for

00:00:16.824 --> 00:00:21.809
us to think about how do we pivot
the organization, how do we shift the way

00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:26.879
that we think as an organization so
that we can create an organization that

00:00:26.879 --> 00:00:32.245
is more poised to positively disrupt
itself in the landscape of disruption.

00:00:32.245 --> 00:00:34.605
[MUSIC]

00:00:34.605 --> 00:00:38.460
&gt;&gt; When a company or an organization
comes to campus to work with us,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:43.310
we've designed the content to meet their
needs in a very human centered way.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:44.850
&gt;&gt; So we are trying to drive innovation,

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.210
we're trying to focus
on the future trends.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:52.240
And the whole program is customized
in a way that works for us.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:58.245
&gt;&gt; The faculty director works very very
closely with the client to determine what

00:00:58.245 --> 00:01:03.055
the content is going to be in the program,
who's going to teach in the program and

00:01:03.055 --> 00:01:06.097
what other kinds of added
benefits there might be.

00:01:06.097 --> 00:01:09.015
&gt;&gt; They want to really make sure
what we're trying to achieve and

00:01:09.015 --> 00:01:12.315
then find the right faculty
to fill those spots for us.

00:01:12.315 --> 00:01:15.290
&gt;&gt; The introduction to the d.school,
they got this

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:19.980
wonderful way of bringing it all together,
getting you to be able to prototype,

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:24.050
being able to learn the principles of
Silicon Valley about failing fast and

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.410
then amplifying what really works.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:30.945
&gt;&gt; The amount of information that faculty
can condense in an 80-minute session and

00:01:30.945 --> 00:01:35.107
the relevancy to what we do day to day
is essential and it happens every time.

00:01:35.107 --> 00:01:38.492
&gt;&gt; They are not theoretical and just
let's talk about what's in the book but

00:01:38.492 --> 00:01:41.330
they make it practical,
they make it actionable.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:45.490
&gt;&gt; In most of our programs, there's
the blend of different kinds of learning.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:48.810
So we may have some case studies,
we may have simulations,

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:53.970
we may have experiential activities and
also a set of online assets that can be

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:59.080
used in a blended program or can be used
in a fully online program for companies.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:04.020
&gt;&gt; We have 12 different organizations
within our company coming to this program,

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:07.050
making those networks and connections.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:11.840
&gt;&gt; We have now developed a common
language across the organization.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.730
&gt;&gt; I know it might sound like a cliche,
but

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:18.220
we don't think that you can afford not
to do the Stanford customized program.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:22.000
&gt;&gt; This program is helping
us transform our company

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.410
the way we want to be at a faster pace.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.423
&gt;&gt; The thing I love about Stanford and
the thing that was so

00:02:27.423 --> 00:02:30.765
appealing to us about Stanford is,
you've got a faculty and

00:02:30.765 --> 00:02:34.456
staff who is focused on actually
making a difference in the world.

00:02:34.456 --> 00:02:38.522
[MUSIC]

